MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SanDisk microSD cards feel like useful spares because I have repeatedly bought removable memory cards, adapters and storage cases; I would still check device compatibility.",
    "The rechargeable AA batteries and charger fit my interest in keeping practical accessories ready to use, as reflected in my earlier charger and battery storage purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My removable memory purchases do not mean I need internal SSDs, desktop RAM or a 16TB drive; those require an upgrade or storage need I have not expressed.",
    "The MacBook sleeve assumes I own a particular laptop, while my case purchase was for a Fire tablet. The keyboard, sound adapter and earbuds also address needs I do not currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying memory cards seems to have been interpreted as interest in any kind of computer storage or memory, even though their uses are quite different.",
    "My frequent electronics accessory purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest broadly related devices without a clear connection to what I use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of cards, cables, mounts and holders suggest that compatibility and a specific practical purpose matter to me.",
    "My camera accessories and recent lens cap purchase provide a stronger reason to suggest useful camera-related accessories than to assume I am upgrading a computer or buying audio equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my need for useful spares, but stretched that into computer upgrades and device-specific accessories without evidence of a current need."
}
